WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.750
{Part A}

00:03.520 --> 00:04.360
Mmhmm...

00:04.360 --> 00:07.650
...suddenly attacked,
and I was in for a rough time!

00:13.330 --> 00:15.370
This way, this way!

00:16.750 --> 00:21.710
Satoshi and friends have come to a certain mountain
that receives perennial snow.

00:21.710 --> 00:23.710
Their goal being...

00:25.260 --> 00:27.010
No chance we’ll get lost now.

00:27.010 --> 00:27.720
Yeah!

00:27.720 --> 00:30.760
The rare spectacle of Koiking
climbing a waterfall!

00:30.760 --> 00:32.970
I’ve always wanted to see it one day!

00:32.970 --> 00:35.560
Mijumaru,
we’re gonna see Koiking!

00:38.600 --> 00:40.650
So cute!

00:46.940 --> 00:47.440
Huh?

00:49.320 --> 00:50.740
It’s completely frozen!

00:50.740 --> 00:52.530
Then we won’t see
any waterfall-climbing...

00:52.530 --> 00:53.580
What?!

00:54.240 --> 00:58.200
Bad luck, huh, Mijumaru?
We don’t get to see the Koiking...

01:03.420 --> 01:04.590
Mijumaru?

01:10.300 --> 01:12.180
Even Pikachu...

01:12.180 --> 01:14.930
Well, if they’re having fun...

01:24.190 --> 01:27.150
(I’ll get Pokémon!)

01:29.110 --> 01:30.650
PocketMonsters

01:29.570 --> 01:30.650
Aim to be a Pokémon Master

01:30.650 --> 01:35.120
Be it fire, water, grass, or forests,

01:35.120 --> 01:39.080
the ground, the clouds, or under that girl’s skirt (Eek!!)

01:39.080 --> 01:43.040
It’s really, really, really, really hard to handle,

01:43.040 --> 01:44.880
but I’m gonna get them all!

01:44.880 --> 01:51.170
I’m gonna get Pokémon!

01:51.170 --> 01:54.140
Masara Town, I bid you goodbye

01:54.140 --> 01:59.020
I’m going on a journey with this little guy (Pikachu)

01:59.020 --> 02:03.020
I’ll win each battle with the moves I’ve mastered,

02:03.020 --> 02:06.690
then head to the next town and make friends along the way!

02:06.690 --> 02:10.900
There’s no way to know for sure

02:10.900 --> 02:14.860
if things will always work out (Got that right!)

02:14.860 --> 02:18.280
But with my companions by my side,

02:18.280 --> 02:24.250
we’ll live life to the fullest!

02:29.130 --> 02:36.470
Ah, I want to be a Pokémon Master so bad

02:36.470 --> 02:40.600
I wanna be one! Gotta be one!

02:40.600 --> 02:44.940
Will be one!

03:40.450 --> 03:41.700
There they are—

03:41.700 --> 03:42.950
Argh!

03:42.950 --> 03:43.950
A Tunbear?!

03:50.630 --> 03:53.960
Does that mean
Tunbear found the hotachi for you?

03:53.960 --> 03:55.340
Thank you!

04:03.100 --> 04:05.100
I’m gonna freeze!

04:11.230 --> 04:13.020
Wait, Tunbear!

04:18.150 --> 04:20.950
Fiarrow, melt the ice!

04:36.210 --> 04:38.630
That’s its ability,
Flame Body, huh?

04:38.630 --> 04:40.220
Thank you, Fiarrow.

04:47.140 --> 04:48.390
Chase after Tunbear.

04:48.810 --> 04:50.730
We’ll catch up to you soon.

04:56.030 --> 04:58.740
Chase after it? Why?

04:58.740 --> 04:59.990
Its eyes...

05:00.700 --> 05:03.490
They looked really sad.

05:04.280 --> 05:05.120
I see.

05:05.120 --> 05:07.290
That <i>is</i> troubling.

05:08.370 --> 05:10.250
Come on out,
Gaogaen, Kabigon!

05:14.040 --> 05:17.840
Kabigon, use Megaton Punch!
Gaogaen, use DD Lariat!

05:29.020 --> 05:31.350
That’s it!
Keep it up and carve out a path!

05:31.350 --> 05:33.770
All right! Foretos,
you help, too!

05:33.770 --> 05:35.360
Us, too! Starmie!

06:12.060 --> 06:15.060
Pikachu! Mijumaru! Fiarrow!

06:16.270 --> 06:17.060
What the...

06:17.820 --> 06:20.070
What happened here?

06:20.070 --> 06:22.320
Gaogaen! Great Blaze!

06:42.800 --> 06:43.590
You okay?!

06:50.100 --> 06:53.060
If Tunbear was behind this, too...

06:53.060 --> 06:54.480
...it’s incredibly strong.

06:54.480 --> 06:57.310
That waterfall must’ve been
its doing, too...

06:58.860 --> 07:00.150
Hang in there!

07:04.320 --> 07:07.490
Tunbear...
Where are you?

07:19.540 --> 07:20.380
Kabigon, return!

07:20.380 --> 07:22.250
Return, Starmie!

07:20.380 --> 07:22.250
Return, Foretos!

07:25.550 --> 07:28.050
Fiarrow, Gaogaen, help!

07:34.680 --> 07:37.440
Nice and warm...

07:38.270 --> 07:42.070
This Tunbear...
It can’t control its ice powers, can it?

07:42.070 --> 07:45.820
You sure?
It made pillars of ice earlier.

07:45.820 --> 07:48.780
Tunbear didn’t <i>mean</i>
to make those.

07:48.780 --> 07:52.200
They’re just made by accident
when it gets scared or frightened.

07:52.580 --> 07:54.700
You’re amazing, Tunbear!

07:55.710 --> 07:57.830
You can freeze so much
with one breath...

07:58.290 --> 08:00.000
...that you’d even surprise Kyurem!

08:00.000 --> 08:02.250
You mean the Legendary Pokémon
of the Isshu Region?

08:02.250 --> 08:05.720
Yeah, it has mighty
ice powers.

08:05.720 --> 08:09.890
Your powers are really amazing!
I love them!

08:09.890 --> 08:12.510
Don’t you wanna learn
how to use ‘em better?

08:13.890 --> 08:16.230
Let’s train together!

08:21.980 --> 08:23.820
Listen up, Tunbear.

08:23.820 --> 08:27.530
Pretty much all Pokémon can
bring out their power using the same trick.

08:27.530 --> 08:29.700
You picture it like
“mmmm...”,

08:29.700 --> 08:32.120
you “fwoosh” it up
inside your body,

08:32.120 --> 08:34.370
take aim, and “bam!”

08:38.000 --> 08:39.960
Yeah, yeah...

08:39.960 --> 08:41.460
See? Looks doable, right?

08:47.970 --> 08:51.260
C’mon, try copying him.
Like this...

08:55.600 --> 08:58.850
That part of Satoshi
hasn’t changed at all.

08:59.690 --> 09:04.190
He still loves Pokémon,
and does everything he can for them.

09:04.190 --> 09:09.780
Yeah. Hopefully Tunbear picks up on
Satoshi’s intentions.

09:09.780 --> 09:14.950
That’s it. Fill your belly up with power,
like “mrrr,” then breathe it out.

09:30.170 --> 09:32.640
You’re doing it,
you’re doing it! Keep it up!

09:48.400 --> 09:50.400
That’s it! Take it slow!

09:58.660 --> 09:59.540
Huh?!

10:17.640 --> 10:19.220
Pocket Monsters!

10:41.910 --> 10:44.000
Thanks, Gaogaen.

10:53.050 --> 10:54.930
This is a tough nut to crack.

10:54.930 --> 10:57.800
I see why the mountain Pokémon
run from it.

10:57.800 --> 11:00.970
Don’t let it get you down,
Tunbear.

11:00.970 --> 11:03.390
So you failed once or twice,
so what?

11:10.730 --> 11:12.860
I get it, Mijumaru!

11:12.860 --> 11:15.820
You’re telling Tunbear to
make a hotachi with its ice, right?

11:15.820 --> 11:20.080
I see! That’ll be good practice
for controlling its powers.

11:32.880 --> 11:34.800
All right, now’s the real start.

11:34.800 --> 11:37.130
Look closely at the hotachi
and concentrate!

11:45.060 --> 11:46.640
Looking good, looking good!

12:23.510 --> 12:25.680
Phew, that was a shock.

12:25.680 --> 12:27.100
Thanks for the help.

12:29.810 --> 12:31.690
You had the parts at the start down.

12:32.110 --> 12:35.320
You’re amazing,
you know that?

12:35.320 --> 12:37.950
So keep training
and don’t give up!

12:46.870 --> 12:48.830
Go for it, Tunbear!

12:48.830 --> 12:51.210
Believe in your power!

12:52.710 --> 12:55.630
Keep it up!
It’s looking like a hotachi!

13:02.850 --> 13:04.810
You did it, Tunbear!

13:04.810 --> 13:06.850
You did it! You did it!
You’re amazing!

13:26.990 --> 13:27.830
Fiarrow!

13:27.830 --> 13:28.950
What power!

13:30.710 --> 13:31.920
Gaogaen...

13:50.020 --> 13:52.020
Tunbear, calm down!

13:52.020 --> 13:55.270
You had it! You were so close!

13:55.270 --> 13:56.650
Don’t worry!

13:57.360 --> 14:00.280
You can do it!
Believe in yourself!

14:08.080 --> 14:09.370
Tunbear!

14:52.450 --> 14:55.210
Thanks, Tunbear. You saved me.

15:00.420 --> 15:01.510
Ow!

15:04.300 --> 15:06.220
Looks like I twisted it.

15:11.140 --> 15:12.850
You can climb out of here.

15:14.270 --> 15:17.860
With your big claws,
those ice walls’ll be a piece of cake!

15:22.360 --> 15:25.530
Tunbear... I can’t move.

15:25.530 --> 15:28.120
So take these guys up with you.

15:31.240 --> 15:34.710
When you get out,
let Takeshi and Kasumi know.

15:49.470 --> 15:51.350
You want me to get on?

15:55.560 --> 15:56.640
Got it.

15:57.640 --> 15:58.730
Thanks.

15:59.980 --> 16:02.230
You gonna be okay, Tunbear?

16:22.840 --> 16:26.670
Fiarrow! Satoshi...
Satoshi fell down here...

16:37.350 --> 16:39.190
That’s how it’s done, Tunbear!

16:56.910 --> 17:01.210
Wow! You just did it!
That’s what you wanted, right?

17:04.090 --> 17:08.420
You controlled your powers!
You found a solution in a crisis!

17:10.680 --> 17:12.550
Now there’s just one thing left to do.

17:13.550 --> 17:16.220
Use your powers to get us out of here!

17:17.310 --> 17:20.440
Don’t worry.
I know you can do it!

17:26.070 --> 17:28.070
All right! Aim over there!

17:36.450 --> 17:37.950
You’re doing it!

17:49.460 --> 17:51.630
Go!

17:56.010 --> 17:57.560
Next, the other side!

18:07.610 --> 18:11.860
That’s it, that’s it! You’ve got it!
Keep climbing higher!

18:27.130 --> 18:30.210
Hey! Kasumi! Takeshi!

18:30.210 --> 18:31.840
Satoshi!

18:33.630 --> 18:36.180
So you’re all okay!

18:36.180 --> 18:37.510
Yeah!

18:38.760 --> 18:43.190
Look!
Tunbear made these ice stairs!

18:43.600 --> 18:44.940
You did it, Tunbear!

18:45.560 --> 18:46.690
Yeah!

18:47.270 --> 18:49.610
You were really cool!

18:52.940 --> 18:54.490
Down I go.

18:54.490 --> 18:57.320
Gah! Ow, ow...

18:57.780 --> 18:59.790
Satoshi, your leg...?

19:00.580 --> 19:02.370
I twisted it...

19:03.210 --> 19:04.580
Let me see.

19:04.580 --> 19:05.870
Thanks.

19:29.770 --> 19:31.110
Give it a try.

20:14.440 --> 20:15.070
You did it!

20:34.840 --> 20:36.880
Did you all see that?!

20:36.880 --> 20:39.220
Tunbear’s become an Ice Master!

20:44.100 --> 20:46.180
They still look worried.

21:23.140 --> 21:24.970
Isn’t that great, Tunbear?

21:32.810 --> 21:37.030
A heart that doesn’t give up...
A heart that believes in oneself...

21:37.030 --> 21:39.690
Tunbear has a bright tomorrow ahead.

21:40.320 --> 21:43.160
And the journey
continues.

21:48.660 --> 21:50.250
How many friends?

21:50.330 --> 21:52.370
Well, I’d say, surely, that must be...

21:52.540 --> 21:54.500
The more the merrier!

21:56.340 --> 21:57.800
Specifically?

21:57.840 --> 21:59.760
Well, plenty, to be precise, exactly...

21:59.880 --> 22:02.010
151 of them!

22:03.800 --> 22:05.260
With a little courage

22:05.350 --> 22:07.390
Oh, great, perfect, with a smile...

22:07.470 --> 22:09.390
I get a new friend!

22:11.270 --> 22:12.940
But yet sometimes

22:13.020 --> 22:14.940
Oh? Distracted, it vanished, dismayed...

22:15.150 --> 22:17.070
They get away instead!

22:18.900 --> 22:22.070
I remember quite well

22:22.610 --> 22:24.610
Meeting each and every one of you

22:26.410 --> 22:29.790
Though we have hurt each other at times

22:29.870 --> 22:31.960
Those were (er...) I forget

22:33.540 --> 22:35.380
I know that there are

22:35.420 --> 22:37.290
many more friends to meet

22:37.380 --> 22:39.420
somewhere out there

22:41.300 --> 22:44.090
151 joys...

22:45.090 --> 22:47.430
151 dreams...

22:48.850 --> 22:51.730
151 memories...

22:52.310 --> 22:55.350
Let’s seek out every one!

23:06.530 --> 23:09.660
Come on!
The Zenigame Fire Squad Show is starting!

23:09.660 --> 23:14.040
Step on up, come and see!
And why not buy some merch while you’re here?

23:14.040 --> 23:15.670
The Zenigame have a show?

23:15.670 --> 23:17.710
I hear it’s really popular these days.

23:17.710 --> 23:18.840
Really?

23:18.840 --> 23:21.800
Let’s go cheer them on
with Fushigidane and Lizardon!

23:23.720 --> 23:27.180
Huh? Zenigame?
What’s wrong?

23:27.180 --> 23:29.100
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

23:29.100 --> 23:31.600
Burn!
The Zenigame Fire Squad!!

23:30.390 --> 23:35.480
The Zenigame Fire Squad!!

23:31.600 --> 23:34.060
Everyone, go and catch Pokémon!
